# Browser Navigation Management System - C++

A C++ Data Structures academic project that simulates browser history, bookmarks, and related pages using linked data structures.

## Project Overview

This project implements a simplified browser navigation and bookmarks management system. It focuses on dynamic memory allocation, pointers, singly linked lists, and doubly linked lists to manage browser-like data.

## Features

- Parse browser data from an input text file
- Store browser history using a doubly linked list
- Store bookmarks using a doubly linked list
- Store related pages using a singly linked list
- Open or create new pages with related pages
- Search browsing history by URL substring
- Delete pages from history and bookmarks
- Remove history older than a specific date
- Find the page with the highest number of related pages
- Display the most recently visited bookmarks
- Remove the least visited bookmark
- Save updated data to an output text file

## Data Structures Used

- Singly Linked List
- Doubly Linked List
- Queue
